## Why This Is Asked
Tests translating CAPA into actionable steps for a concrete, repeatable risk. It targets beginner CAPA skills without vague theory.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model design
- Lifecycle/state machine
- Evidence capture and traceability
- Lightweight REST API for CAPAs
- Canary-based remediation and region-aware metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let cas = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = {...req.body, id: Date.now().toString(), status: 'detected'};
  cas.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the CAPA workflow end-to-end?
- How would you enforce secret masking in build logs across agents?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

